<title>INDIA: BSE figures of India carry forward trade.</title>
<headline>BSE figures of India carry forward trade.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the latest data, for the top 10 stocks by value, released by the Bombay Stock Exchange (BSE) for the carry forward or &quot;badla&quot; account ended November 2.</p>
<p>SCRIP		  SETTLEMENT  AV BADLA  QTY    VALUE    % BADLA</p>
<p>			 RATE				 (RS MLN)</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>State Bank	   225	   0.62     431250  97.03    14.37</p>
<p>Tata Steel	   177	   0.52     504600  89.31    15.32</p>
<p>Reliance	     195	   0.55     321350  62.66    14.71</p>
<p>ACC		   1510	   4.04	22110  33.39    13.95</p>
<p>L&amp;T		    220	   0.51     114100  25.10    12.09</p>
<p>Tata Power	   121	   0.32     187550  22.69    13.79</p>
<p>Tata Engg	    410	   0.92	53250  21.83    11.70</p>
<p>MTNL		   225	   0.29	70300  15.82     6.72</p>
<p>ICICI		   59	   0.15     218500  12.89    13.26</p>
<p>IPCL		   111	   0.19     104800  11.63     8.93</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The average badla charges work out to 13.42 percent on an annualised basis against 10.66 percent in the previous carry forward account ended Oct 26.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
